# kokoro-js (the free voice) brings in onnxruntime-node, whose install script on Linux x64 (the
# Workers Builds machine) downloads ONNX Runtime's CUDA (GPU) files from GitHub. The site never
# runs it in Node, let alone on a GPU, and when that download fails (a 404 for v1.21.0) the whole
# `npm clean-install` fails and nothing deploys. Skipping it changes nothing the app uses.
onnxruntime-node-install-cuda=skip
